From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 025] panvk: fillModeNonSolid via GPU polygon kernel on gpu_prerast
Generated-by: LLM

Purpose: DXVK requires fillModeNonSolid (D3D11 FILL_WIREFRAME). Valhall has
 no polygon-mode raster state, so a pipeline with polygonMode LINE/POINT
 compiles a third VS variant (GPU_POLYGON compute kernel) next to the
 gpu_prerast lowered/passthrough variants. Per draw, the lowered VS writes
 post-VS records on the GPU, the polygon kernel assembles triangles
 (list/strip/fan, primitive restart, instancing), computes facing from the
 clip-space determinant (front face, negative viewport height), applies
 cullMode and emits line (AB,BC,CA) or point indices plus an indirect draw
 into the device arena; the passthrough VS then draws LINES/POINTS
 indexed-indirect with restart. No CPU readback.
 Fixes carried with it: pipeline hash includes the non-solid state (the VS
 variant set depends on it); build_dcd_flags takes the drawn primitive;
 the polygon kernel waits for the lowered VS scoreboard slots; lowered VS
 record and index stores are bounded by arena capacity (ABI 2, arena 32MB,
 65536 invocations).
 Limits: dynamic polygon mode stays unexposed; draws above arena capacity,
 multi-draw indirect and indirect-count, and shaders with side effects keep
 the filled hardware path.
Source/Reference: Vulkan spec 28.x polygon mode / basic polygon
 rasterization (area sign, cull); fork idea GunaCharanTeja a966c0d
 (fill-mode part rewritten on the gpu_prerast path)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (0xb8a31030, PAN_ARCH 11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b
Dependencies: csf-v11/024
Validation test: tests/dxvk/vulkan/fill-mode/fill_mode.c (17/17 IDVS and
 PANVK_DEBUG=gpu_prerast, pixel-exact against a GPU LINE_LIST/POINT_LIST
 reference)

